WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:16.738
mayor might cancel the parade?"

2
00:00:17.118 --> 00:00:18.059
Henry exclaimed.

3
00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:22.700
"Why? Does he think that threat on the website was serious?

4
00:00:23.681 --> 00:00:24.341
Or did Mr.

5
00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:26.602
Fleming talk him into canceling the parade?"

6
00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:28.303
Jackson shrugged.

7
00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:29.283
"I don't know.

8
00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:31.144
I didn't hear it from the mayor.

9
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:33.652
I was talking to Miss Bishop.

10
00:00:34.273 --> 00:00:35.273
She's the one who told me."

11
00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:37.714
"How did she hear about it?"

12
00:00:38.014 --> 00:00:38.774
Henry asked.

13
00:00:39.814 --> 00:00:40.494
"I'm not sure.

14
00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:44.356
I couldn't talk to her for very long because I had to leave for a meeting."

15
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:46.476
Jackson checked his watch.

16
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.257
"Speaking of which, I've got to get inside or I'll be late."

17
00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:53.158
He hurried into the newspaper office.

18
00:00:54.479 --> 00:00:56.499
Henry thought about what Jackson had just said.

19
00:00:57.439 --> 00:00:59.080
Should Miss Bishop be a suspect?

20
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.923
She seemed determined to win the contest for best float.

21
00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.065
She seemed especially interested in beating Mrs.

22
00:01:06.125 --> 00:01:09.688
Sweet. Could Miss Bishop be the one who'd tampered with Mrs.

23
00:01:09.728 --> 00:01:10.429
Sweet's float?

24
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.092
Then Henry remembered the threatening website message.

25
00:01:15.013 --> 00:01:16.975
Why would Miss Bishop do something like that?

26
00:01:17.935 --> 00:01:21.739
If she wanted to win, it didn't make sense for her to try to shut down the whole

27
00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:25.502
parade. Henry started walking his bike down the sidewalk.

28
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:27.744
The jewelry store was up ahead.

29
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.842
He decided to stop in and talk to Miss Bishop.

30
00:01:31.903 --> 00:01:35.366
A little bell over the door jingled when Henry entered the jewelry store.

31
00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:38.989
Nobody was inside except Miss Bishop.

32
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.092
She was wiping a display case with a rag.

33
00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:45.355
"Oh, hello, Henry," she said.

34
00:01:45.375 --> 00:01:48.938
"Did you come to buy your mother a diamond necklace?"

35
00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:53.381
Henry smiled politely as Miss Bishop laughed at her own joke.

36
00:01:54.362 --> 00:01:56.084
"No, sorry," he said.

37
00:01:56.848 --> 00:02:00.311
"Our lemonade business doesn't make quite enough money for that."

38
00:02:01.232 --> 00:02:02.153
"Too bad."

39
00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.156
Miss Bishop smiled, and then sighed.

40
00:02:05.176 --> 00:02:08.158
"I could really use some new customers.

41
00:02:08.999 --> 00:02:10.700
Business has been slow this summer."

42
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.123
"Oh," Henry said.

43
00:02:13.143 --> 00:02:14.664
"That's a shame."

44
00:02:14.684 --> 00:02:20.769
"Yes, that's why I decided to enter a float in the parade this year," Miss Bishop said.

45
00:02:20.789 --> 00:02:23.392
"I thought it would be good publicity.

46
00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.042
And if I win the popular vote contest, I'll get to be on TV.

47
00:02:28.902 --> 00:02:31.223
That's like winning a free ad for my store."

48
00:02:31.243 --> 00:02:36.366
"You must be worried about the mayor canceling the parade then," Henry said.

49
00:02:36.386 --> 00:02:39.447
"What?" Miss Bishop looked alarmed.

50
00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:42.228
"The mayor is canceling the parade?

51
00:02:42.488 --> 00:02:43.389
Who told you that?"

52
00:02:43.409 --> 00:02:47.791
"Jackson, the reporter from the newspaper," Henry said.

53
00:02:47.811 --> 00:02:49.992
"He said you told him that."

54
00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:52.505
"I told him no such thing!"

55
00:02:52.825 --> 00:02:53.966
Miss Bishop exclaimed.

56
00:02:53.986 --> 00:02:56.747
"He must be thinking of someone else.

57
00:02:57.388 --> 00:02:58.408
Do you think it's true?

58
00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:01.350
Why would the mayor cancel the parade?"

59
00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.311
Henry wasn't sure what to say for a moment.

60
00:03:05.272 --> 00:03:07.533
He was confused by Miss Bishop's reaction.

61
00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.135
She seemed very surprised and upset.

62
00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:13.696
"Was Jackson here talking to you earlier?"

63
00:03:13.957 --> 00:03:14.737
Henry asked.

64
00:03:15.838 --> 00:03:16.778
Miss Bishop nodded.

65
00:03:16.798 --> 00:03:21.841
"Yes, he stopped by a few minutes ago, and we had a nice chat.

66
00:03:22.761 --> 00:03:25.002
I was telling him about my business problems."

67
00:03:25.022 --> 00:03:28.343
"And you didn't say anything about the parade?"

68
00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:29.324
Henry asked.

69
00:03:30.364 --> 00:03:36.927
"I did mention the parade, but I didn't say anything about the mayor canceling it," Miss Bishop said.

70
00:03:36.947 --> 00:03:41.749
"I told Jackson that I was hoping my float would bring me more customers.

71
00:03:42.809 --> 00:03:45.470
And that if it didn't, I might have to shut down my store."

72
00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:49.272
"Oh." Suddenly Henry had a brainstorm.

73
00:03:50.328 --> 00:03:51.669
"I bet I know what happened.

74
00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:55.871
You told Jackson you might have to shut down your store.

75
00:03:56.872 --> 00:04:00.653
But Jackson thought you were talking about the mayor shutting down the parade."

76
00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:04.255
"Hmm." Miss Bishop looked unsure.

77
00:04:04.275 --> 00:04:06.496
"That seems odd.

78
00:04:07.097 --> 00:04:09.418
But Jackson did seem to be in a hurry.

79
00:04:10.539 --> 00:04:12.340
Maybe he wasn't listening closely."

80
00:04:15.324 --> 00:04:20.047
As Henry left the store, he wondered if Jackson had really misunderstood Miss Bishop's comment.

81
00:04:21.168 --> 00:04:24.329
The young reporter was always looking for exciting news stories.

82
00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.172
What if he was the one trying to get the parade shut down?

83
00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:32.314
That would definitely give Jackson an interesting story to write about.

84
00:04:33.415 --> 00:04:36.697
Henry thought some more about his theory as he biked toward Maggie's house.

85
00:04:37.937 --> 00:04:42.160
Jackson could have posted that threatening message on the website just as easily as anyone else.

86
00:04:43.284 --> 00:04:44.584
He could have broken into Mrs.

87
00:04:44.624 --> 00:04:45.245
Sweet's shed.

88
00:04:46.065 --> 00:04:51.947
And he was definitely the one spreading the rumor about the parade being canceled—either by accident or on

89
00:04:52.027 --> 00:05:00.169
purpose. When Henry reached Maggie's house, Maggie and Cole were putting away their craft supplies.

90
00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:02.650
"What took you so long?"

91
00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:03.850
Maggie asked Henry.

92
00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.691
"It's dinnertime.

93
00:05:06.051 --> 00:05:07.931
We'll have to finish the float in the morning."

94
00:05:07.951 --> 00:05:10.272
"Sorry," Henry said.

95
00:05:11.452 --> 00:05:15.494
"I ended up doing a little extra investigating on my way home from the auto shop."

96
00:05:16.454 --> 00:05:18.275
He told his friends about his trip to town.

97
00:05:19.376 --> 00:05:23.518
When he explained his theory about Jackson being the culprit, Cole looked worried.

98
00:05:23.538 --> 00:05:29.580
"If Jackson is a suspect now, we can't count on him to solve the mystery," he said.

99
00:05:30.761 --> 00:05:31.501
Henry nodded.

100
00:05:31.521 --> 00:05:34.283
"You know what that means," he said.

101
00:05:34.303 --> 00:05:37.144
"We'll have to solve it ourselves!"
